  "story": {
    "what_changed": "Seasonal inundation expanded over 420 km² during peak wet discharge. Open water extent grew by 64% while flooded marsh and canopied swamp vegetation expanded by 115%.",
    "drivers": "Heavy seasonal monsoon rainfall leading to river overbanking across low-gradient alluvial plains.",
    "caveats": "Instrument data gap between 2026-07-27 and 2026-08-10 means the initial rising limb of the flood was not recorded. Candidate classifications use calibrated thresholding, not ground truth.",
    "radar_explainer": "Smooth open water specularly reflects the satellite microwave pulse away, appearing pitch black (< -18 dB). In contrast, water standing beneath tree trunks creates a double-bounce corner reflector effect, producing abnormally high HH backscatter (> -5 dB)."
  },
